# Example ReRDMFT input file: water molecule, evaluating the MULLER
# (Muller/Buijse-Baerends, Occ_opt/JK_only.h) JK-only RDMFT functional
# on the converged approximate X2C-HF spinors -- same idea as
# water_muller.inp/co-sto-3g_muller.inp's own NON_REL/C4_DHF runs, just
# for X2C (see README.md's "X2C decoupling and X2C-HF" section): the
# converged X2C-HF orbitals/MO-basis integrals are held FIXED, initial
# fractional occupations are generated (OCCUPATION_INIT PROPORTIONAL by
# default), FUNCTIONAL is evaluated on them, and the occupations are
# then further OPTIMIZED at those same fixed orbitals via Occ_opt/SQP.h
# -- printed right after the X2C-HF Hessian_opt cross-check section.
# Like NON_REL (and unlike C4_DHF), every X2C-HF spinor competes for
# occupation, since X2C's own decoupling already eliminated the
# negative-energy branch entirely. Kramers partners (adjacent even/odd
# indices) are confirmed to always receive the SAME optimized
# occupation, exactly as for C4_DHF's own spinors.
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL MULLER
DEBUG TRUE

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
